ensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $3.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $66K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Prologis, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $125.1B market cap on $8.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 199% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.9929297914492876},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $8.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-8035050.0},{"text":"Payout ratio of 93% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 27% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings Growth & Price Strength Make Prologis (PLD) a Stock to Watch","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029418/earnings-growth-price-strength-make-prologis-pld-a-stock-to-watch?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_focus_list-3029418","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Could Tightening Supply Mean For Prologis (PLD) Through 2027?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/could-tightening-supply-mean-prologis-011346500.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794532426.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]}